      "message": "It is not related to this change, but I would like to point out that the current implementation causes the warning about duplicate of the I2C address. I\u0027m not sure how we should handle this, since the `nuvoton,nct38xx-gpio` driver is already in Zephyr. I think the ultimate solution would be something like this:\n```\n\ttcpc_port0: nct38xx@70 {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"nuvoton,nct38xx\";\n\t\treg \u003d \u003c0x70\u003e;\n\t\t...\n\n        \tnct3808_0_P1: nct3808_0_P1 {\n\t\t\tcompatible \u003d \"nuvoton,nct38xx-gpio-port\";\n\t        \t...\n\t        \tioex_port1: gpio@0 {\n\t\t        \tcompatible \u003d \"nuvoton,nct38xx-gpio-port\";\n\t\t\t        reg \u003d \u003c0x0\u003e;\n\t\t\t        ...\n\t\t\t};\n\t\t};\n        \ttcpc: tcpc-port0 {\n\t\t\tcompatible \u003d \"nuvoton,nct38xx-tcpc\";\n\t        \t...\n\t\t};\n\n\t};\n```\nBut at the moment I don\u0027t know what to do.",
